WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.960
- Welcome back everybody.

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.180
Our next guest's life has
been quite the journey.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.760
He overcame addiction
and living in his car

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.620
to become America's motivator

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.810
for healthy living and
weight loss, incredible.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:10.740
He's an author

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.870
and was the host of "Extreme Weight Loss."

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.660
Now he has a new podcast
called "I Needed That"

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.900
all about improving your
life on the inside and out.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.580
It's perfect if you're already trying

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.470
to reignite your New Year's resolutions

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.210
that you may have already quit by now.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.617
Let's welcome Chris Powell, everybody.

00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:28.453
(audience cheering)

00:00:28.453 --> 00:00:30.870
So, I'm gonna say this podcast,

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.910
is it kinda like a reset for you?

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:33.743
- It is.

00:00:33.743 --> 00:00:36.180
I consider it kind of my
second mountain actually

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.320
after the show.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.900
You know, I spent 20 years
helping people find themselves

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:40.739
through fitness

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:42.900
and I actually went through my own

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.469
difficult mental health battle.

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:47.250
Went through a divorce and saw...

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:48.300
- Oh, me too, yeah.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.600
- It really, I found myself
in a really dark place.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.820
I went through six
therapists in five years,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.210
and I full extreme ownership of it,

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:00.090
I became the worst version of myself.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.580
And I just realized that
it was time to separate

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.260
and as I went through that though,

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.680
it was just emptiness and
loneliness and all of that.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.640
And so, sure enough, I ended up

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.560
realizing the power of mental health

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:14.730
when it comes to transformation.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.230
And so yes, like this whole thing

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:19.050
it really is the second
mountain for myself

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.570
just because I can't
have this conversation

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.910
about transformation, about
physical health and all that

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:25.410
without talking about mental health

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:28.380
because it's, when you talk,
- It's powerful.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.370
- It's everything in one,

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.220
it's a holistic approach
to transformation now.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.540
And so, and I didn't realize that

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.130
until going through my own battle

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:39.870
and utilizing different tools
like breathing, gratitude,

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.790
and talking about it with other people.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:42.990
I can't stress that enough.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.900
And that's where the podcast
has become so important for me

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.070
'cause it really is,

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:48.870
it's kind of part of my recovery.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.430
- Oh, talking for me is same, I mean,

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:51.263
obviously I have a talk show.

00:01:51.263 --> 00:01:53.496
But I just, it's the same thing for me.

00:01:53.496 --> 00:01:56.730
That's how I almost figure it out

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:58.020
is by talking with people.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.300
I learn about myself while hearing myself

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.820
say something aloud like,
"Wait, did I mean that?

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.140
Or did I, what, what does that?"

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.300
And also, with mental health

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.340
I think people think like,
"Oh, you know, you're sad."

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.220
The hardest part is you
don't know you're depressed

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.590
or sad sometimes, you don't catch it

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:16.590
and you can't recognize that at first.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:18.360
And so, that's when I talk to someone too

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.740
like during my divorce

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.080
and still do because it's
really healthy, I think,

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.670
to have somebody outside your circle.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.020
But you launched, I wanna talk about this

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.574
'cause you also launched a nonprofit.

00:02:26.574 --> 00:02:29.010
So can you tell us a
bit about that and why?

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.360
- So, service.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.200
You know, service,

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.180
especially when you're going
through a difficult time,

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.100
you spend so much time
thinking about yourself,

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.260
but you realize like how powerful it is

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.610
when you start to serve others.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:39.990
And that was one of the biggest things

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.090
that really helped me find myself again.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:45.150
And it was in the middle of
the pandemic and quarantine.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.320
People weren't moving,

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.960
and obviously mental health
issues were through the roof.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.270
And I was so inspired by
something that happened in Japan.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.530
This is a crazy story.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:53.940
Back in 1928.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.790
They mandated three and a
half minutes of movement

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:57.630
done to music.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.490
It's movement and music together.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.142
And it was the same 13
movements done to the same music

00:03:01.142 --> 00:03:05.970
every day, every factory, every
school, every corporation.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.800
They all moved at the same time.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.770
And in one generation, Japan
became the healthiest country

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.330
in the world and they united.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:13.163
- What?

00:03:13.163 --> 00:03:16.110
- Yes, it's called rajio taiso,
it means radio calisthenics.

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:17.670
It's powerful.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.684
It changed the country.

00:03:18.684 --> 00:03:19.710
- It's 13 movements

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.390
and it's only like a couple
minutes every morning?

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:22.770
- It's three and a half minutes long.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.050
And I was so inspired by that.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.900
And sure enough, here
we are, 94 years later,

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.780
27 million still do rajio
taiso every single day

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.730
and they continue to be the
healthiest country in the world.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.770
And I was like, we need this now.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:35.935
- I need this now, what?

00:03:35.935 --> 00:03:37.410
- Yes, we do.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.150
- I wanna know these movements, yeah.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.830
- I started my nonprofit Move 1 Million,

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:41.940
and it's two and a half minutes

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:43.860
because who's got three and a
half minutes nowadays, right?

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.140
So it's 13 movements just to pay tribute

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.030
to the 13 from Japan.

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.440
But yeah, I created the music.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.180
I actually wrote and
played the music for it.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:54.744
And I take us, it's a total
body warmup, top to bottom.

00:03:54.744 --> 00:03:57.810
And I mean, it's absolutely,

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.430
the impact that it's had.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.840
Schools have started adopting it.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.250
We launched it in 2021.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.200
Schools have been adopting it, hospitals.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.050
We've got 100,000 people
moving in 71 countries now

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.550
for two and a half minutes a day.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.140
And it's been incredible.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.310
- I think that's incredible.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.110
It's so simple, yet effective.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:13.943
- That's it.
- Yeah.

00:04:13.943 --> 00:04:15.720
- Lower the barrier of
entry and sure enough

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:16.553
and everyone can do it.

00:04:16.553 --> 00:04:19.050
And a body in motion
tends to remain in motion.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:19.883
- I'm gonna do this

00:04:19.883 --> 00:04:20.716
and you're gonna come back

00:04:20.716 --> 00:04:22.760
and I'm gonna be like, so changed.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:23.593
- Oh, I love it.

00:04:23.593 --> 00:04:25.200
In fact, have me back and
I wanna move everybody.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.033
We'll have a blast.

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.360
Two and a half minutes.
- I'm down for that.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.590
I think that's cool.
- Let's go.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.870
- Well, Chris's podcast "I Needed That"

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.370
co-hosted by Matthew Blades

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.920
is available on all streaming
platforms, everybody.

